439 - How Far From Home?
 / 
Key: Db
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 439
Topic: Early Advent - 

Verse 1:
[Db]How far from home? I [Gb]asked, as [Db]on I [Ab]bent my steps—th[Db]e watchman spake:
[Db]"The long, dark night is [Gb]almost [Db]gone, The [Ab]morning soon will [Db]break.
Then [Ab]weep no more, but [Db]speed thy flight, With [Ab]Hope's bright star thy [Db]guiding ray,
[Db]Till thou shalt reach the [Gb]realms of [Db]light, In [Ab]everlasting [Db]day."

Verse 2:
[Db]I [Gb]asked [Db]the warrior [Ab]on [Db]the field;
[Db]This [Gb]was [Db]his [Ab]soul-inspiring [Db]song:
[Ab]"With [Db]courage, bold, [Ab]the sword [Db]I'll wield,
[Db]The [Gb]battle [Db]is [Ab]not [Db]long.
[Db]Then [Gb]weep [Db]no more, [Ab]but [Db]well endure
[Db]The [Gb]conflict, [Db]till thy [Ab]work [Db]is done;
[Ab]For this [Db]we know, [Ab]the prize [Db]is sure,
[Db][Gb]When [Db]victory [Ab]is [Db]won."

Verse 3:
[Db]I [Gb]asked [Db]again; earth, [Ab]sea, [Db]and sun
[Db]Seemed, [Gb]with [Db]one voice, [Ab]to [Db]make reply:
[Ab]"Time's [Db]wasting sands [Ab]are [Db]nearly run,
[Db][Gb]Eternity [Db][Ab]is [Db]nigh.
[Db]Then [Gb]weep [Db]no [Ab]more-with [Db]warning tones,
[Db]Portentous [Gb]signs [Db]are [Ab]thickening [Db]round,
[Ab]The [Db]whole [Ab]creation, [Db]waiting, groans,
[Db]To [Gb]hear [Db]the [Ab]trumpet [Db]sound."

Verse 4:
[Db]Not [Gb]far [Db]from home! [Ab]O [Db]blessed thought!
[Db]The [Gb]traveler's [Db]lonely [Ab]heart [Db]to cheer;
[Ab]Which [Db]oft a [Ab]healing balm [Db]has brought,
[Db]And [Gb]dried [Db]the [Ab]mourner's [Db]tear.
[Db]Then [Gb]weep no [Db]more, [Ab]since we [Db]shall meet
[Db]Where [Gb]weary [Db]footsteps [Ab]never [Db]roam-
[Ab]Our [Db]trails past, [Ab]our [Db]joys complete,
[Db]Safe [Gb]in [Db]our [Ab]Father's [Db]home.
